WEBVTT

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:13.320
Romeo's Blue Skies

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:13.320
"To the Sky..."

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:17.960
<i>Overlooking the rows of houses and stores</i>

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:22.370
<i>from the highest vantage,</i>

00:00:23.030 --> 00:00:27.480
<i>Such things as tears and sadness</i>

00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:31.620
<i>will quickly vanish</i>

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:37.180
<i>The birds, wind, and sunshine...</i>

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:41.370
<i>...all are your friends</i>

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:46.440
<i>I'll carry this dream farther than far</i>

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:51.530
<i>...no matter the distance...</i>

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:58.290
<i>I long to fly freely</i>

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:02.570
<i>through the blue sky in my heart...</i>

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:05.500
<i>The far distant blue sky</i>

00:01:05.610 --> 00:01:12.950
<i>It flows into tomorrow</i>

00:01:19.090 --> 00:01:25.290
Takara Fansubs

00:01:27.330 --> 00:01:28.760
<i>Christmas.</i>

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:34.600
<i>Romeo had spent a wonderful week at Dr. Casella's house.</i>

00:01:35.010 --> 00:01:41.760
<i>Dr. Casella had opened the door to the world of knowledge for Romeo.</i>

00:01:42.730 --> 00:01:48.240
<i>A tiny dream took spark in Romeo's heart, which was now turning to the future.</i>

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:53.240
Episode 33:

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:53.240
To the Sky! On Wings of Freedom!

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:07.500
<i>Spring had come to the city of Milan.</i>

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:14.080
<i>Spring, the season that all the chimney sweeps had dreamt of.</i>

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:22.680
<i>Their contracts would be ending, and their long difficult labor coming to an end.  </i>

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:27.590
Finally...
- Yeah.

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:34.750
<i>Yes... at last, the contracts of Dante, Michaelo, Antonio and Romeo end today,</i>

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:38.280
<i>...and they are returning home together.</i>

00:02:38.730 --> 00:02:40.440
All right! It's finally over.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:44.750
You heard right, Piccolo. It's over.

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:50.760
So, climbing onto these rooftops...

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:56.890
...is also over.

00:02:56.920 --> 00:02:58.510
Romeo!

00:02:59.730 --> 00:03:02.070
Romeo, quit goofing off!

00:03:02.290 --> 00:03:04.800
You've still got work to do!

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:07.560
Coming! Right away.

00:03:08.350 --> 00:03:10.360
Can't turn your head for one minute with that boy.

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:14.760
He never finishes cleaning the windows and mopping.

00:03:14.770 --> 00:03:19.120
The windows look spotless to me.
- Spotless my foot!

00:03:22.710 --> 00:03:24.370
Spotless.

00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:25.880
Mrs. Rossi...

00:03:26.330 --> 00:03:29.370
what would you like me to do next?

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:32.310
Let's see now...

00:03:32.410 --> 00:03:37.400
Figure that out yourself!
- Hey Edda, Romeo's contract is over today.

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:38.890
Starting this morning he's free.

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:42.860
It's a waste not to use him for all we can!

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:49.980
How much do you think it cost to...
- ...get this boy? It cost us 82 lira!

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:55.660
Go and get ready now, Romeo.
- Yessir.

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:03.570
I remember when you first came to my house.

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:06.560
You've become a lot stronger since then.

00:04:06.590 --> 00:04:09.230
It's finally time to say goodbye, boss...

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:12.680
I'm sorry for making your stay here so hard.

00:04:13.490 --> 00:04:17.300
I won't forget this room you made for me.

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:21.170
How can I put it, boss?
You're like... a father to me.

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:27.600
Romeo, in all my years sweeping chimneys,

00:04:27.920 --> 00:04:33.780
...I never had a partner as plucky as you, and probably never will.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:42.660
Anzelmo, it's me.

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:44.260
Come in.

00:04:44.770 --> 00:04:48.160
I'm going now. Goodbye, Anzelmo.

00:04:48.860 --> 00:04:53.200
I know without you telling me! So go!

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:56.680
I've still got a little work to do.

00:04:56.900 --> 00:04:58.400
Work...?

00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:01.420
To make up with you.

00:05:03.130 --> 00:05:07.710
Don't strain yourself.
You haven't really forgiven me.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:10.190
It's forgotten.

00:05:12.550 --> 00:05:13.280
Go!

00:05:15.280 --> 00:05:18.500
Then... I'll leave this here as a sign of reconciliation.

00:05:18.530 --> 00:05:20.780
I don't have anything else to give you.

00:05:22.670 --> 00:05:24.360
See you, Anzelmo.

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:27.330
I hope things go well for you.

00:05:38.920 --> 00:05:41.400
Boss... Mrs. Rossi...

00:05:41.420 --> 00:05:44.850
Goodbye! Thank you for everything!

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:47.860
Thank you, Romeo! Thank you!

00:05:49.430 --> 00:05:50.900
Goodbye.

00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:55.540
Let's go.
- OK.

00:05:58.170 --> 00:05:59.860
R... Romeo.

00:06:02.440 --> 00:06:04.120
Edda, are you...

00:06:05.490 --> 00:06:10.240
Ah! Glad to be rid of that nuisance!

00:06:12.290 --> 00:06:16.200
Goodbye, Romeo. Have a happy life.

00:06:19.240 --> 00:06:24.400
The long hard winter's finally over... It's goodbye Milan!

00:06:24.410 --> 00:06:26.520
If only Alfredo could be with us.

00:06:27.090 --> 00:06:31.620
After surviving that storm on the lake, and making it here together...

00:06:31.750 --> 00:06:35.020
Alfredo's the only one who didn't make it out of Milan.

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:39.770
Bianca will be here too, so don't worry. Alfredo won't be lonely.

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:45.140
That's right... So she'll be living with Dr. Casella now.

00:06:45.160 --> 00:06:49.000
And they both said they'd accompany us halfway there.

00:06:54.250 --> 00:06:55.800
A sign of reconciliation.

00:06:56.790 --> 00:06:59.410
I hope things go well for you.

00:07:04.660 --> 00:07:09.020
You...! You're not getting the last laugh.

00:07:10.250 --> 00:07:15.150
Dad, when's the next assistant coming? Dad! Dad!!

00:07:17.340 --> 00:07:18.840
What is it, Romeo?

00:07:19.090 --> 00:07:20.910
Luini, the God of Death.

00:07:22.220 --> 00:07:25.910
<i>It was the situation they had all been in six months ago.</i>

00:07:26.700 --> 00:07:34.860
<i>New boys being brought in place of Romeo and the others who were now free.</i>

00:07:35.140 --> 00:07:37.200
<i>Realizing this dark truth,</i>

00:07:37.220 --> 00:07:44.340
<i>...their hearts were filled with violent anger and deep sadness.</i>

00:07:47.310 --> 00:07:52.100
Alfredo, remember when I promised to put a flower in my hair?

00:07:52.760 --> 00:07:54.100
Well, I've done it.

00:07:56.880 --> 00:07:59.510
Are you watching, Alfredo?

00:07:59.770 --> 00:08:03.360
You were kind. Maybe you would have said I looked nice.

00:08:03.390 --> 00:08:04.870
You look fabulous!

00:08:05.530 --> 00:08:10.520
I want to show you to everyone in town, you're so cute!

00:08:11.070 --> 00:08:13.130
How long have you guys been there?

00:08:14.670 --> 00:08:15.330
Nikita!

00:08:18.070 --> 00:08:22.000
Look after Alfredo for us, will you?

00:08:22.120 --> 00:08:23.270
Romeo.

00:08:25.710 --> 00:08:29.400
Don't worry, I'll take good care of Alfredo's grave.

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:30.640
Thank you.

00:08:31.470 --> 00:08:34.600
Romeo!
- He-ey!

00:08:34.650 --> 00:08:36.490
We came to see you off.

00:08:37.220 --> 00:08:39.920
Dr. Casella is waiting at the graveyard entrance.

00:08:39.940 --> 00:08:40.560
All right.

00:08:42.050 --> 00:08:46.770
You three guys will be the only ones left here now...

00:08:47.750 --> 00:08:49.450
Don't sweat it.

00:08:49.480 --> 00:08:52.330
Our contracts will be over soon, then we'll get to go home too.

00:08:53.770 --> 00:09:00.900
<i>Giuliano, Bartolino and Paulino had already completed their contracts,</i>

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:04.400
<i>...and had gone home together.</i>

00:09:05.730 --> 00:09:07.880
So that's how it is.

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:11.420
We'll finally have some peace in this town.

00:09:11.450 --> 00:09:13.880
Giovanni, you've come too!

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:17.950
We've come to make sure you leave, you pest.

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:22.890
I'm leaving. But I have one last favor to ask you.

00:09:23.630 --> 00:09:25.200
Last favor?

00:09:25.230 --> 00:09:28.210
Yes.
- Go ahead.

00:09:28.210 --> 00:09:31.660
I want the Wolf Pack and the Black Brothers to join forces.

00:09:31.970 --> 00:09:34.780
Join forces...
- With chimney sweeps?

00:09:35.130 --> 00:09:37.840
Yes. Once we're gone,

00:09:37.870 --> 00:09:43.320
...other kids will be brought in as chimney sweeps every year.

00:09:44.340 --> 00:09:47.630
I want you to live in peace with them.

00:09:49.470 --> 00:09:51.640
Listen closely, Romeo.

00:09:51.930 --> 00:09:56.150
We've been sold by the adults, made to suffer.

00:09:56.850 --> 00:10:00.150
But there are many children in the world just like us.

00:10:01.570 --> 00:10:03.400
I know... a time will come...

00:10:03.950 --> 00:10:07.970
...when we will all be able to learn and live in freedom.

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:11.860
Learn and live in freedom...

00:10:11.880 --> 00:10:16.280
Right. We're going to build the new age... all of us, together!

00:10:17.150 --> 00:10:19.780
Fulfill our dreams... together!

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:25.600
I want to help fulfill the dreams Alfredo never had a chance to fulfill.

00:10:25.660 --> 00:10:29.060
I'll need your help to do that, Giovanni.

00:10:30.550 --> 00:10:32.050
Let's do it...

00:10:32.630 --> 00:10:37.710
a pact between the Wolf Pack and the Black Brothers.

00:10:37.750 --> 00:10:41.070
Sounds good to me. I'm all for it.

00:10:41.100 --> 00:10:42.250
Me too.

00:10:42.280 --> 00:10:46.280
What's the hold-up, Giovanni? That's not like you.

00:10:46.320 --> 00:10:50.160
I was planning on this from the start.
- Then, Giovanni...?

00:10:50.190 --> 00:10:55.400
Yes. From now on the Black Brothers are our friends.

00:10:55.420 --> 00:10:56.420
Giovanni!

00:10:56.900 --> 00:10:58.240
That's the ticket.

00:10:58.270 --> 00:11:00.750
A peace pact!
- Friends in peace.

00:11:02.670 --> 00:11:04.890
Never again will we fight.

00:11:04.920 --> 00:11:06.410
Never again.

00:11:07.100 --> 00:11:08.510
Swear on Alfredo's name.

00:11:09.380 --> 00:11:11.720
On Alfredo's name.

00:11:12.940 --> 00:11:20.070
Alfredo. The peace you so loved... has finally come.

00:11:29.190 --> 00:11:32.510
Take care, tomboy.
- You too, buttinsky.

00:11:32.520 --> 00:11:35.200
Romeo, I won't forget our fights.

00:11:35.860 --> 00:11:39.270
Me neither.
Take care, everyone.

00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:42.460
You too, Romeo.
- I won't forget about you.

00:11:42.480 --> 00:11:43.520
Me too.

00:11:44.770 --> 00:11:47.710
Let's get going.
- Yes.

00:11:48.810 --> 00:11:51.700
The Black Brothers will always be together.

00:11:51.710 --> 00:11:55.230
Always be together!

00:11:59.450 --> 00:12:05.150
Goodbye! Take care!

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:09.560
Romeo!
- Romeo!

00:12:15.670 --> 00:12:18.320
So he's gone.

00:12:19.370 --> 00:12:22.050
<i>Romeo, I'll keep my promise.</i>

00:12:22.090 --> 00:12:25.340
<i>I'll take care of Alfredo.</i>

00:12:28.420 --> 00:12:32.900
Hm...
Never noticed the sky was so pretty...

00:12:35.810 --> 00:12:39.840
I'll never get anything done today.
I think I'll go have a belt instead.

00:12:40.470 --> 00:12:42.680
Drinking again!

00:12:42.700 --> 00:12:46.680
Romeo, go bring that
good-for-nothing back! Romeo!

00:12:49.040 --> 00:12:53.280
This house has suddenly gotten so empty.

00:12:54.160 --> 00:12:57.870
Mother, Mother!
I'm hungry.

00:12:58.930 --> 00:13:00.360
Mother?

00:13:03.940 --> 00:13:06.880
This is the last we'll see of Milan.

00:13:07.580 --> 00:13:12.750
You can see the roofs we climbed onto.
- We might never come back.

00:13:12.950 --> 00:13:16.100
Let's burn this sight into our memories.

00:13:18.170 --> 00:13:22.390
<i>The sky of Milan, which had seen Romeo's tears and smiles...</i>

00:13:29.840 --> 00:13:34.440
<i>It was of such a deep, blue color that it singed the eyes.</i>

00:13:35.690 --> 00:13:41.880
<i>Romeo would never forget that blue.</i>

00:13:50.810 --> 00:13:54.720
Lago Maggiore!
- You'll all be home pretty soon.

00:14:05.370 --> 00:14:07.720
The Alps... my home.

00:14:14.420 --> 00:14:18.890
Romeo, we had tough times, but we also had fun.

00:14:18.910 --> 00:14:21.160
I was so happy to meet you all.

00:14:21.640 --> 00:14:23.810
Me too, Michaelo.

00:14:24.760 --> 00:14:26.320
See you, Antonio.

00:14:27.480 --> 00:14:31.360
I won't forget our times in Milan, even when I grow up.

00:14:31.390 --> 00:14:35.630
Me neither.
- I'll punch you out if you do.

00:14:36.870 --> 00:14:40.000
No matter how far apart we are, we're brothers!

00:14:40.020 --> 00:14:41.790
Brothers!

00:14:45.500 --> 00:14:48.350
Bye, Romeo! Bye, Dante!

00:14:48.400 --> 00:14:51.410
Take care, Michaelo! So long!

00:14:51.430 --> 00:14:54.910
Don't be a crybaby forever, Michaelo!

00:14:56.480 --> 00:14:57.870
Let's go, Michaelo.

00:15:06.970 --> 00:15:10.330
<i>Goodbye, Michaelo, Antonio.</i>

00:15:24.170 --> 00:15:28.360
Dante.
- Guess it's time for me to go.

00:15:28.390 --> 00:15:31.000
Bianca, take care of yourself.
- You too, Dante.

00:15:31.690 --> 00:15:33.660
No need to worry about me!

00:15:35.940 --> 00:15:38.850
Thanks for everything, Doctor.

00:15:38.970 --> 00:15:42.160
Please watch yourself, Dante.

00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:45.480
You act a bit reckless sometimes.

00:15:45.520 --> 00:15:49.490
OK... But that's what makes me interesting!

00:15:49.520 --> 00:15:50.030
Dante.

00:15:53.240 --> 00:15:55.170
It's time to say goodbye.

00:15:55.840 --> 00:15:57.600
We've been through a lot together.

00:16:00.930 --> 00:16:05.680
I want to say "Till we meet again."...
But life's not that simple.

00:16:06.180 --> 00:16:11.430
Now we both know things probably won't turn out the way we want.

00:16:11.550 --> 00:16:14.200
We might never see each other again.

00:16:22.330 --> 00:16:23.610
Just kidding.

00:16:24.870 --> 00:16:28.960
What's it matter...
Well, have a nice life, Romeo!

00:16:30.610 --> 00:16:31.980
Dante!

00:16:34.210 --> 00:16:35.760
We'll meet again somewhere!

00:16:37.540 --> 00:16:39.180
I know it!

00:16:48.220 --> 00:16:50.810
So long, Mr. Nice Guy!

00:16:59.150 --> 00:17:01.120
<i>We'll meet again.</i>

00:17:08.200 --> 00:17:12.090
We'll be going now too, Romeo.

00:17:12.210 --> 00:17:15.120
Thank you very much, Doctor.

00:17:16.390 --> 00:17:20.880
I won't forget about when you taught me how to write.

00:17:21.410 --> 00:17:24.790
You wrote out "Romeo" for me.

00:17:24.840 --> 00:17:26.890
Those were the first letters I learned.

00:17:27.590 --> 00:17:30.970
You're like a different person now.

00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:32.560
Your efforts paid off.

00:17:33.050 --> 00:17:35.810
It wasn't just me.

00:17:35.840 --> 00:17:40.110
It's because of them... because the Black Brothers were there with me.

00:17:42.830 --> 00:17:47.110
Starting today, let's call everyone here the Black Brothers!

00:17:47.410 --> 00:17:49.150
Black Brothers?

00:17:49.180 --> 00:17:51.850
Because we're all brothers here!

00:17:51.910 --> 00:17:53.590
The Black Brothers fraternity.

00:17:54.150 --> 00:17:57.070
We'll help each other out.

00:17:57.160 --> 00:17:59.090
We'll share sadness, happiness...

00:17:59.650 --> 00:18:04.080
And we'll overcome all hardships by working together!

00:18:04.430 --> 00:18:06.810
We're family!

00:18:06.840 --> 00:18:08.750
We're family!

00:18:14.110 --> 00:18:16.680
Well... I have to go now.

00:18:19.130 --> 00:18:22.070
Can I come to your village to play sometime?

00:18:22.120 --> 00:18:24.870
Sure. Of course.
- I'll write, too.

00:18:24.880 --> 00:18:26.790
Me too, I promise.

00:18:28.100 --> 00:18:33.720
I finally understand the dreams my brother passed on to you.

00:18:33.750 --> 00:18:34.620
Bianca.

00:18:35.120 --> 00:18:38.640
You both really and truly believe in each other.

00:18:38.850 --> 00:18:40.970
You'll be friends forever.

00:18:41.000 --> 00:18:45.080
Yes! Alfredo's dreams are my dreams.

00:18:48.200 --> 00:18:50.190
<i>Romeo had returned home alone,</i>

00:18:50.210 --> 00:18:55.110
...just as he had been at the beginning of this long journey.

00:18:56.770 --> 00:18:59.100
Bye, Romeo!

00:19:00.570 --> 00:19:04.400
<i>Having met and been separated from many people...</i>

00:19:04.690 --> 00:19:08.190
<i>...having experienced true happiness and overcome sadness,</i>

00:19:08.490 --> 00:19:12.200
<i>...Romeo sensed that he had grown a great deal.</i>

00:19:13.730 --> 00:19:18.280
<i>His eyes now gazed steadily at tomorrow.</i>

00:19:18.850 --> 00:19:21.420
Look, Piccolo!
It's Sonogno village!

00:19:24.260 --> 00:19:27.930
<i>Alfredo, I'm back, finally.</i>

00:19:28.210 --> 00:19:32.090
<i>I don't know what I can do yet...</i>

00:19:32.300 --> 00:19:36.560
<i>But I'm going to fulfill my dreams, I know it... with you.</i>

00:19:38.070 --> 00:19:40.350
Let's go home, Piccolo.

00:19:40.860 --> 00:19:48.860
<i>Talking to the white clouds floating by,</i>

00:19:40.860 --> 00:19:48.860
<i>Nagareru shiroi kumo ni itsudemo hanashi kakeru</i>

00:19:50.090 --> 00:19:59.120
<i>In my heart I hear a tiny voice answer.</i>

00:19:50.090 --> 00:19:59.120
<i>Kotaeru koe ga mune ni kikoerun da shinjitara</i>

00:19:59.840 --> 00:20:08.720
<i>Tiny now, compared to the vastness of the sky.</i>

00:19:59.840 --> 00:20:08.720
<i>Hiroi sora ni kurabete ima wa chiisana</i>

00:20:08.720 --> 00:20:13.520
<i>One day, one day,</i>

00:20:08.720 --> 00:20:13.520
<i>Boku no yume wo itsuka itsuka</i>

00:20:12.690 --> 00:20:18.460
<i>Finally, his long journey was ended.</i>

00:20:13.550 --> 00:20:18.440
<i>My dreams will fill the sky,</i>

00:20:13.550 --> 00:20:18.440
<i>Sorajuu ni hirogaru yo</i>

00:20:20.100 --> 00:20:29.640
<i>Hands spread wide to the blue sky, I want to become one</i>

00:20:20.100 --> 00:20:29.640
<i>Ryoute wo blue sky nobashite hitotsu ni naritai</i>

00:20:29.650 --> 00:20:39.760
<i>In the soft embrace of the glimmering blue sky.</i>

00:20:29.650 --> 00:20:39.760
<i>Kagayaku blue sky sora ni yasashiku dakarenagara</i>

00:20:40.840 --> 00:20:47.000
<i>Ten years later, Romeo, having worked while going to school,</i>

00:20:47.040 --> 00:20:49.760
<i>...has graduated and is teaching children.</i>

00:20:49.960 --> 00:20:54.130
<i>Acting as a tiny light to guide the poor and the weak,</i>

00:20:54.470 --> 00:20:58.460
<i>...Romeo has taken the first step towards realizing his dream.</i>

00:21:02.950 --> 00:21:10.910
<i>Romeo and Bianca married, and they named their first child Alfredo.</i>

00:21:13.570 --> 00:21:20.560
<i>The practice of selling children as chimney sweeps is no more.</i>

00:21:21.270 --> 00:21:29.110
<i>But now more than ever, children all over the world lead difficult lives...</i>

00:21:29.140 --> 00:21:32.130
<i>...due to poverty and war.</i>

00:21:33.650 --> 00:21:36.930
<i>But Romeo never stops hoping that one day,</i>

00:21:37.330 --> 00:21:44.670
<i>...all children will be able to run free under the blue sky.</i>

00:21:46.560 --> 00:21:49.860
The End

00:21:57.130 --> 00:21:58.420
I'm John.

00:21:58.440 --> 00:22:01.350
I'm always with my beloved Lassie!

00:22:01.420 --> 00:22:04.670
We're close friends, right?

00:22:05.410 --> 00:22:07.840
New show: "Famous Dog Lassie"

00:22:07.880 --> 00:22:13.250
14 Jan 7:30 p.m. on-air. Stay tuned!

00:22:14.510 --> 00:22:17.700
<i>"Si Si Ciao ~ On These Roman Roofs"</i>

00:22:27.180 --> 00:22:31.280
<i>Si Si Ciao, why do the good times</i>

00:22:31.380 --> 00:22:35.580
<i>seem to end so soon?</i>

00:22:35.780 --> 00:22:39.780
<i>Si Si Ciao, we're all friends</i>

00:22:39.980 --> 00:22:43.980
<i>Let's meet again on these Roman roofs</i>

00:22:44.590 --> 00:22:48.890
<i>Your laughing voice dances</i>

00:22:48.890 --> 00:22:52.790
<i>Once again in the sky</i>

00:22:53.190 --> 00:23:00.090
<i>Your pocket bursting with memories</i>

00:23:01.790 --> 00:23:05.690
<i>Si Si Ciao, goodbye but for now</i>

00:23:05.890 --> 00:23:09.890
<i>Let's meet again on these Roman roofs</i>
